course: dictionary
lesson: 1351
title: Cancel: call it off, or make it count for nothing
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: «Our school trip was cancelled because of the snow.» The trip was planned, but now it will not happen. When an event is called off, it is cancelled.
explain: «I need to cancel my ticket for the match.» Here cancel means to stop a booking or order so that it no longer counts. Words like ticket and match are the clues.
explain: In maths, cancel can mean making a fraction simpler by dividing the top and bottom by the same number. Two things can also cancel out, like plus 5 and minus 5, which together make 0.
explain: «Noise-cancelling headphones listen to the noise and play the opposite wave, so the push and the pull cancel out.» Read the whole sentence to find the meaning: the two waves go against each other and nothing is left.
fact: Cancel is a verb: cancel, cancels, cancelled, cancelling.
fact: «Cancelled» can mean that a planned event will not happen, such as a match or a trip.
fact: In maths, cancelling a fraction means dividing the top and bottom by the same number, so 6/8 becomes 3/4.
fact: «Cancel out» means two things have equal and opposite effects, so together they make nothing.
fact: A good check is to swap your meaning into the sentence and see if it still makes sense.
exercise: «Our school trip was cancelled because of the snow.» What does cancelled mean here? | Made much bigger | *Called off, so it will not happen | Moved to a sunny day | Found again
exercise: In maths, you cancel 6/8 to make 3/4. What do you do to the top and bottom? | Take away only the top | *Divide both by the same number | Add 10 to both | Turn both upside down
exercise: «Noise-cancelling headphones ... the push and the pull cancel out.» What does cancel out mean? | Two things get much louder | One thing is fixed by the other | Both things start moving faster | *Two opposite things make nothing together
test: «I cancelled my ticket for the match.» What does cancelled mean? | Bought again | Lost | *Stopped, so it no longer counts | Drawn in colour
test: What do plus 5 and minus 5 do when they cancel out? | They make 10 | They make minus 10 | They make 5 | *They make 0
exam: Which word means to stop an order or booking so that it no longer counts? | expand | repeat | *cancel | arrive
